nsformation $T: R^{5} → R^{5}$. If $nullity(T) = 3$ then $rank(T) =$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 false] [17592186188923 1071 "Consider a linear transformation $T:{R}^{5}\\to {R}^{5}.$ If $\\text{nullity}(T)=3$ then $\\text{rank}(T)=$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186188923 1074 "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $T:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{n},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)+\\text{nullity}(T)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given transformation, we have $n=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(T)+\\text{nullity}(T) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(T)+3 & =5 \\\\ \\text{rank}(T) & =5-3 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186188930 1068 #edb/ref 17592186187626 13194139533445 17592186045585 false] [17592186188930 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363953 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186188930 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186188930 1071 "Find $\\text{nullity}(T)$ given that $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ and \n\n$$\n\\text{Im}(T)={[x,y,z]^{T}\\,:\\,-x+z=0}.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186188930 1071 "Find $nullity(T)$ given that $T: R^{3} → R^{3}$ and\n$Im(T) = {[x, y, z]^{T}: - x + z = 0}$." 13194139533445 17592186045585 false] [17592186188930 1074 "Solving $-x+z=0$ for $z,$ we get $z=x.$ Therefore, any vector from $\\text{Im}(T)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ x\\end{aligned}]=x{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{1}}+y{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}.$ Therefore, $\\text{rank}(T)=2.$ \n\nFinally, according the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T) & =3-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186198378 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362999 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186198378 1038 #edb/ref 17592