85 true] [17592186362482 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362482 1080 #uuid "853597e9-85d5-5c98-99a7-5367188bd89b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362483 1081 "A half-plane that passes through the $z$-axis" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362483 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362483 1084 #uuid "71c382ac-1eac-5abc-95df-6def14541172" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362484 1081 "A sphere" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362484 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362484 1084 #uuid "6e74e9a3-6670-5588-9023-b750f1f372ed" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362485 1081 "A plane that is parallel to the $xy$-plane" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362485 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362485 1084 #uuid "eaddfd2d-93c8-5fee-8bad-9d3d4cccb9d5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362486 1081 "A half-cone" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362486 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362486 1084 #uuid "7a2bde51-684c-5e48-b2a6-b08aed5f08e9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362487 1081 "A circular cylinder" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362487 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362487 1084 #uuid "c424832f-b884-5818-8b53-81947b568c74" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362488 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362489 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362488 1069 "q-104980" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362488 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362488 1071 "The function $f(x,y)$ has Hessian matrix\n\n$$\n{∇}^{2}f(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2(y-3) & 2(x+1) \\\\ 2(x+1) & (y-3)^{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand has a stationary point at $(-1,3).$ If $H$ denotes the Hessian determinant of $f,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $H(-1,3)<0$\n- $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(-1,3)>0$\n- The second partial derivative test is inconclusive" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362488 1072 #uuid "a2adfa73-7e18-5d5d-8163-694e5efa8a14" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362488 1074 "The second partial derivative test states that if $a\\in {R}^{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x,y)$ with Hessian determinant $H(a),$ then:\n\n- If $H(a)>0,$ then:\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a local maximum at $a$;\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)>0,$ then $f$ has a local minimum at $a.$\n\n- If $H(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a saddle point at $a.$\n\n- If $H(a)=0,$ then the second partial derivative test is inconclusive.\n\nEvaluating the Hessian at $(-1,3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{∇}^{2}f(-1,3)=[\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{2}+2(3-3) & 2(-1+1) \\\\ 2(-1+1) & (3-3)^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The Hessian determinant is\n\n$$\nH(-1,3)=det({∇}^{2}f(-1,3))=1(0)-0(0)=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true because\n\n$$\n\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(-1,3)=1>0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true because $H(-1,3)=0,$ so the second partial derivative test is inconclusive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362490 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362491 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362489 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362494 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362489 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362489 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362489 1079 #edb