86045585 true] [17592186362652 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362653 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362652 1069 "q-111774" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362652 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362652 1071 "Consider the standard matrices of three linear transformations shown below. Which of the transformations map ${R}^{2}$ onto $(0,0)?$\n\n$$\n{T}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{T}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{T}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362652 1072 #uuid "47539370-0241-5c5a-be9d-00783bbc307e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362652 1074 "Given a linear transformation over ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ we have the following:\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto ${R}^{2}$ if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=2,$ i.e., $T$ is nonsingular.\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=1.$\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto $(0,0)$ if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=0,$ i.e., $T$ is the zero matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- ${T}_{1}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto $(0,0)$ since ${T}_{1}$ is the zero matrix, i.e. $\\text{rank}({T}_{1})=0.$\n\n- ${T}_{2}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto ${R}^{2}.$ Indeed, ${T}_{2}$ is a nonsingular matrix, i.e. $\\text{rank}({T}_{2})=2.$\n\n- ${T}_{3}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line. Notice that the columns of ${T}_{3}$ are linearly dependent but it's not the zero matrix. So, $\\text{rank}({T}_{3})=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362654 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362655 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362656 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362657 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362658 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362653 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362653 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362653 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362656 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362653 1080 #uuid "03d7334c-0ff0-5553-b1c2-886da95f9dc0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362654 1081 "${T}_{2}$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362654 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362654 1084 #uuid "709c3c3c-624d-59ae-844b-5e91f0bcb6bd" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362655 1081 "${T}_{1}$, ${T}_{2}$, and ${T}_{3}$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362655 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362655 1084 #uuid "270d29d1-c33c-5b5b-9833-a4772f59100b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362656 1081 "${T}_{1}$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362656 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362656 1084 #uuid "b0f8a93e-70fd-5d0e-9eab-8677a1c620ff" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362657 1081 "${T}_{3}$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362657 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362657 1084 #uuid "ddc5620c-fba6-5c6e-aab3-b60ca4539af0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362658 1081 "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362658 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362658 1084 #uuid "828b5c4b-a420-5f01-bee8-d7e332049730" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362659 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362660 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362659 1069 "q-113501" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362659 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362659 1071 "The domain of the function $f(x)=\\frac{4x+3}{5x+2k}$ is $(-\\infty ,\\frac{2}{5})\\cup (\\frac{2}{5},\\infty ).$ What is the value of $k?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362659 1072 #uuid "ee16459a-bf12-529f-aa3b-cc89f5e9cb99" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362659 1074 "A reciprocal function is defined for all values of $x$ except for those that make the denominator zero. So, to find the domain, we must exclude all values that make the denominator zero.\n\nSetting the denominator equal to zero and solving, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2k & =0 \\\\ 5x & =-2k \\\\ x & =-\\frac{2k}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the point that must be excluded from the domain is $x=-\\frac{2k}{5}.$ \n\nOn the other hand, we can see that $x=\\frac{2}{5}$ is excluded from the domain. Equating this to $-\\frac{2k}{5},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2k}{5} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{k}{5} & =-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362661 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362662 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362663 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362664 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362665 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362660 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362660 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362660 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362665 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362660 1080 #uuid "6c3b44ec-e362-5848-b757-e1a30a3bc178" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362661 1081 "-5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362661 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362661 1084 #uuid "a2016816-28e8-5d51-9785-1496f42addb7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362662 1081 "3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362662 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362662 1084 #uuid "a1103bae-8319-57e0-97ad-c5f4b71339b0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362663 1081 "2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362663 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362663 1084 #uuid "58d4f932-503e-5417-a6ef-0f99b77003fd" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362664 1081 "1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362664 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362664 1084 #uuid "7872df49-3602-579a-81a7-9757623ee8c0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362665 1081 "-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362665 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362665 1084 #uuid "51e49929-146d-5950-b7fb-a559e7e56524" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362666 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362667 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362666 1069 "q-114240" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362666 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362666 1071 "${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{x}-x-1}=$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362666 1072 #uuid "52b4d998-08c9-5b8e-9e74-1ff6d7cb2d7c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362666 1074 "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{x}-x-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[{x}^{2}]^{′}}{[{e}^{x}-x-1]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2x}{{e}^{x}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x-1+{e}^{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2x}{{e}^{x}-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[2x]^{′}}{[{e}^{x}-1]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362667 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362668 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362667 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362669 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362667 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362670 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362667 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362671 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362667 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362672 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362667 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362667 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362667 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362669 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362667 1080 #uuid "69e5b2f1-392f-5128-8f9c-fc9d2c8d33cc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362668 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362668 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362668 1084 #uuid "49851532-30c7-5fc0-9a39-59ad1c1338ba" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362669 1081 "2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362669 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362669 1084 #uuid "839ff078-d526-5536-a690-24a2142f02a5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362670 1081 "1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362670 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362670 1084 #uuid "76a5277b-e0ab-5edc-8236-c78fdd77539b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362671 1081 "-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362671 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362671 1084 #uuid "f97e7d20-8b29-5dc1-bb6d-71fa6f940136" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362672 1081 "-2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362672 1083 #edb/ref 17592