relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=15-3t,$ where $t>0$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=14\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=1\\,\\text{s},$ calculate the maximum velocity ${v}_{\\text{max}}$ of the particle and determine the time when the particle reaches its maximum velocity." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362694 1072 #uuid "3b21641d-ae30-55b8-ba2d-d86f82ac4d9c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362694 1074 "The extrema of the velocity $v$ occur at the critical points of $v.$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=a(t),$ to find the times where $v$ is a maximum, we just need to solve $a(t)=0$ and test each solution using the first or second derivative test.\n\nSolving $a(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =0 \\\\ 15-3t & =0 \\\\ t & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the extremum of the velocity function occurs when $t=5\\,\\text{s}.$\n\nWe now test the extreme value using the second derivative test. For this, we find the second derivative of $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}v}{\\text{d}{t}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(a(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(15-3t) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${v}^{″}(5)<0,$ we conclude that the velocity is maximized when $t=5\\,\\text{s}.$\n\nNow, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (15-3t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =15t-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $v(1)=14.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15(1)-\\frac{3}{2}(1)^{2}+C & =14 \\\\ C & =\\frac{3}{2}-1\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{1}{2}+15t-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}.$\n\nFinally, we calculate the maximum velocity:\n\n$$\n{v}_{\\text{max}}=v(5)=\\frac{1}{2}+15(5)-\\frac{3}{2}(5)^{2}=38\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362695 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362696 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362695 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362697 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362695 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362698 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362695 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362699 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362695 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362700 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362695 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362695 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362695 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362697 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362695 1080 #uuid "3d2fe126-317a-5c9d-9ee4-ef8f3e825381" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362696 1081 "{v}_{\\text{max}}=37.5\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s},\\,t=5\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362696 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362696 1084 #uuid "9aeba58e-2480-5903-9203-c20e42f54324" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362697 1081 "{v}_{\\text{max}}=38\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s},\\,t=5\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362697 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362697 1084 #uuid "8a0694e3-2d64-5b6e-8fdf-99e203f46da9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362698 1081 "{v}_{\\text{max}}=14\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s},\\,t=1\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362698 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362698 1084 #uuid "145e16e0-16a5-5047-a144-2563881addf1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362699 1081 "{v}_{\\text{max}}=24.5\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s},\\,t=2\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362699 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 