6362725 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362725 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362725 1084 #uuid "cb699b26-8700-53e1-89a0-b258c6ab715c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362726 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362726 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362726 1084 #uuid "a9a37d2a-7bd5-528f-9255-1cf91b830b77" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362728 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1069 "q-126714" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1071 "![](images/0b/0b69c23833e64df8fa1c938bb87b6cfcf8a67018fb1af73424d26e64e49ee4f5.png)\n\nConsider the arc of the curve $y=2x-{x}^{2}$ that lies in the first quadrant between its $x$-intercepts. What integral gives the area of the surface generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis?" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1072 #uuid "3bc1fc15-2cf1-50bc-bcb4-3171e2123e4d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362727 1074 "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi x\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $y=f(x),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we find where the curve intersects the $x$-axis by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ x(2-x) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=0$ to $x=2.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-{x}^{2})=2-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\sqrt{1+{(2-2x)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\sqrt{1+4-8x+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\sqrt{5-8x+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362728 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362729 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362728 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362730 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362728 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362731 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362728 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362732 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362728 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362733 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362728 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362728 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362728 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362732 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362728 1080 #uuid "ee10a059-aa95-593d-a0f7-1d56ebfcbda6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362729 1081 "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x-{x}^{2})\\sqrt{5-4x+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362729 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362729 1084 #uuid "e2a94f5e-8e68-549e-a8ed-83dc42cea847" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362730 1081 "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\sqrt{5-4x+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362730 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362730 1084 #uuid "ac0fd73d-dd4f-5970-ad42-69fec767d6be" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362731 1081 "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{5-8x+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362