452" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362810 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362810 1071 "Find the orthogonal projection of the vector $x$ onto the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362810 1072 #uuid "b15ae07d-6779-551f-ab28-55256b58c480" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362810 1074 "First, notice that $v$ and $w$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362811 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362812 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362811 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362813 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362811 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362814 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362811 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362815 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362811 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362816 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362811 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362811 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362811 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362812 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362811 1080 #uuid "0051ff91-5982-5f79-8021-15f6e5a79345" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362812 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362812 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362812 1084 #uuid "1c8cc9b5-4fea-51be-8530-093f28bb182d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362813 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362813 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362813 1084 #uuid "d8437765-1667-5b4a-a2d4-519d741042f9" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362814 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362814 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362814 1084 #uuid "80156ccd-7acc-5a08-958d-43e718870bf6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362815 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362815 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362815 1084 #uuid "46e97d17-2170-52e4-bae8-f1a4b26c06f1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362816 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362816 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362816 1084 #uuid "bb6446d2-ce20-5814-95a8-6fcf987d8011" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362817 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362818 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362817 1069 "q-140554" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362817 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362817 1071 "Which of the following equations define a non-empty set of points in the ${x}_{1}{x}_{2}$-plane?\n\n- ${x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}=-1$\n- ${x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}=0$\n- ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=0$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362817 1072 #uuid "d7ec5e81-6115-5881-b6f7-16bb9226da5a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362817 1074 "Let's examine each of the equations in turn.\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}=-1$ defines a non-empty set. It represents the hyperbola ${x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2}=1.$\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}=0$ defines a non-empty set. It represents a parabola that opens in the direction of the negative ${x}_{2}$-axis in the ${x}_{1}{x}_{2}$-plane.\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=0$ defines a non-empty set. It represents a single point $(0,0)$ in the ${x}_{1}{x}_{2}$-plane.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362819 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362820 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362821 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362822 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362823 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362819 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362818 1080 #uuid "713649dd-841d-595d-ad2c-1d706d7c2e1a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362819 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362819 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362819 1084 #uuid "ebbc61b3-da42-52b4-8b9a-1c8bfc6e51d4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362820 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362820 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362820 1084 #uuid "e57b11cb-0a00-5658-98f3-d87f6a7775f5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362821 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362821 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362821 1084 #uuid "259d1b4b-cb8c-5458-acca-8cb674f94596" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362822 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362822 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362822 1084 #uuid "e7d2ca84-53fb-576d-85e4-ed21ca559e67" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362823 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362823 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362823 1084 #uuid "088b9f24-a8df-521a-bfbe-dbaa748a06e6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362824 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362825 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362824 1069 "q-140557" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362824 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362824 1071 "What type of quadratic curve is defined by the following equation?\n\n$$\n4{x}_{1}^{2}+16{x}_{1}=-7\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362824 1072 #uuid "59ff20d8-dfd7-5f57-8dd7-676de1c62793" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362824 1074 "First, we complete the squares for the variable ${x}_{1}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}^{2}+16{x}_{1} & =-7 \\\\ 4({x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}+4-4) & =-7 \\\\ 4({x}_{1}+2)^{2}-16 & =-7 \\\\ 4({x}_{1}+2)^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, performing the change of variable\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}={x}_{1}+2,\n$$\n\nwe get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}_{1}^{2} & =9 \\\\ {y}_{1}^{2} & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents the pair of parallel lines ${y}_{1}=\\frac{3}{2}$ and ${y}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362826 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362827 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362828 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362829 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362830 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362829 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362825 1080 #uuid "fa02b4c6-e130-5f57-94ca-7875e4b08f0a" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362826 1081 "A pair of intersecting lines" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362826 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362826 1084 #uuid "34b2f2de-15d8-5ab1-b00e-502c92c80ede" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362827 1081 "An empty set" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362827 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362827 1084 #uuid "4a07a491-9472-50b7-8caa-2551ff3dffe7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362828 1081 "A parabola" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362828 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362828 1084 #uuid "d3feab1f-710d-5f7d-916d-6dccaf02ac63" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362829 1081 "A pair of parallel lines" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362829 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362829 1084 #uuid "626e74b3-c07c-5db1-8452-88dfd54f5e59" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362830 1081 "A hyperbola" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362830 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362830 1084 #uuid "83cebc46-9365-5662-a211-861041f69667" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362831 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362832 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362831 1069 "q-140561" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362831 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362831 1071 "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{61}} & \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{61}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{61}} & \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{61}}\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{13} & 2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind $|\\text{det}(PQ)|$ given that $P$ is an orthogonal matrix." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362831 1072 #uuid "46fe346a-e4ad-51c6-9905-aaf9356199fc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362831 1074 "We use the following facts: \n\n- The determinant of a product is equal to the product of the determinants.\n\n- The determinant of an orthogonal matrix $P$ is equal to $\\pm 1.$\n\nApplying these ideas, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\text{det}(PQ)| & =|\\text{det}(P)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|(\\pm 1)\\cdot \\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\pm 1|\\cdot |\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\text{det}(Q)| \\\\  & =|\\sqrt{13}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}-0\\cdot 2| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{65}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362832 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362833 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362832 1