13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362866 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362866 1071 "Find the orthogonal projection matrix that maps $x\\in {R}^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362866 1072 #uuid "3897ca8e-c190-5166-8001-b5cc763dcea3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362866 1074 "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nMoreover, ${u}_{i}\\cdot {u}_{i}^{T}$ is the projection matrix corresponding to ${u}_{i}.$\n\nFirst, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to $\\lambda =2.$ Computing $A-2I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-2I & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖v‖=\\sqrt{2}.$ Dividing $v$ by its norm, we obtain the normalized eigenvector: \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, the required orthogonal projection matrix is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {u}^{T} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362867 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362868 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362867 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362869 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362867 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362870 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362867 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362871 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362867 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362872 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362867 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362867 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362867 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362868 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362867 1080 #uuid "1feaaa2b-9f91-5604-bad3-f9a41903fec2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362868 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362868 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362868 1084 #uuid "259bc7f0-def1-5dbe-84fa-df884b75de5b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362869 1081 "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362869 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362869 1084 #uuid "4ede6774-72a7-5e72-98ce-278b61c0729e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362870