5 true] [17592186362908 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362908 1071 "The number of people $N$ infected by a particular virus increases with time. The rate of change of the number of infected people is proportional to the square of the number of infected people. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of people infected by the virus at time $t?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362908 1072 #uuid "141b5a5d-ddd8-5877-bf13-99c64ae12afa" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362908 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **number of people infected** by a particular virus $N$ **increases** with time. The **rate** of change of the number of infected people is **proportional** to the **square of the number of people infected** by the virus.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *number of infected people* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *number of infected people squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}∝{N}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number of infected people *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k{N}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362910 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362911 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362912 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362913 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362909 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362914 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362909 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362909 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362909 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362914 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362909 1080 #uuid "02644996-55c0-5996-b3fc-cfdd30efd999" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362910 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-k{N}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362910 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362910 1084 #uuid "0f90381d-5e2f-5094-98f4-35628b46b4d1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362911 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k\\sqrt{N},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362911 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362911 1084 #uuid "482fbf95-8b59-579a-90e6-50d8a87c4afe" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362912 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{N},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362912 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362912 1084 #uuid "c89b41bf-d528-52ea-9315-071885864a4b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362913 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{N}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362913 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362913 1084 #uuid "9c587e50-36d3-57d6-916e-8900b45e04ed" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362914 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k{N}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362914 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362914 1084 #uuid "1513a057-3e2d-5151-bd82-f056466791bc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362915 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362916 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362915 1069 "q-143683" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362915 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362915 1071 "Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- If $A$ is *any* matrix, then ${A}^{3}$ is always symmetric.\n- The sum of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric.\n- The difference of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362915 1072 #uuid "b742394a-cffb-5df9-9fbd-181d0debffeb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362915 1074 "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, consider the matrix \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nHowever, ${A}^{3}$ is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any two symmetric matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}+{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any two symmetric matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A-B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}-{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A-B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362917 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362916 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362918 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362916 1075 #edb/ref 1759218636