86362986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362987 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362988 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362989 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362990 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362991 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362986 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362986 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362986 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362988 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362986 1080 #uuid "41b5e0a4-cf00-583c-a984-8ae1dfc82f1b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362987 1081 "t\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,5)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362987 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362987 1084 #uuid "c7611792-a531-5ef8-866d-9af52225a5e8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362988 1081 "t\\in (-\\infty ,5)\\cup (5,\\infty )" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362988 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362988 1084 #uuid "1b37c0f1-d847-518b-bccd-485ec07f49e5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362989 1081 "t\\in (0,5)\\cup (5,\\infty )" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362989 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362989 1084 #uuid "6231c3a6-ecce-5339-9c7f-4ad1e13d47b4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362990 1081 "t\\in (5,\\infty )" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362990 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362990 1084 #uuid "22541586-6b50-5cf1-bea8-390226c78195" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362991 1081 "t\\in (-5,\\infty )" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362991 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362991 1084 #uuid "35887ca3-a94b-506e-8020-8cda97d2a2f0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362992 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362993 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362992 1069 "q-162490" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362992 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362992 1071 "![](images/22/22058df7ac75e085e1dc352736d1abf289e80d68f340ee63687e69d18e9b23c2.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz.$ The region of integration is shown above.\n\n*Hint: Change the order of integration to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z.$*" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362992 1072 #uuid "07a226bd-3963-51a9-8f33-263f394aef39" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362992 1074 "We cannot integrate the given integral because we cannot find a simple antiderivative of the integrand. So, we change the order of integration.\n\nWe wish to find the limits of integration ${u}_{1}(x,z),$ ${u}_{2}(x,z),$ ${v}_{1}(z),$ ${v}_{2}(z),$ $a,$ and $b$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(z)}^{{v}_{2}(z)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the region of integration $R$ can be written as a type II region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi ,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\pi ,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le y}\n$$\n\nThe region $R$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/c5/c5eec166cdce2fa4be756aa144b6a802082def0374c2b6150794cb2f0f22f1a6.png)\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z$ to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z,$ we write $R$ as a type III region and its projection $D$ onto the $xz$-plane as a type II *plane* region.\n\nTo visualize this, imagine firing an arrow through the region parallel to the $y$-axis and in the direction of increasing $y,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a93024f817970869a3dcef831abc2515fe14efac5ec9dd778701d063b8351d.png)\n\nThe arrow enters the region through the left boundary and leaves through the right boundary:\n\n- The left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x,z),$ is\n\n$$\nx=y\\,⟹\\,y=x.\n$$\n\n- The right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=\\pi .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,x\\le y\\le \\pi },\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/ec/ec3bc5a58b5521286388294b97e1449bb41548004477d6d4555c9b7b917f2bd7.png)\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type II plane region in the $xz$-plane with the right curve given by $x=\\pi .$\n\n![](images/20/205c88cdd0b8a2676bc8396760095fa238ae39acd3660ed5aba2df3726161410.png)\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{x}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}[{\\int }_{x}^{\\pi }\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}[y]_{x}^{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\pi -x}\\cdot (\\pi -x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-(-1-1)\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2[z]_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362993 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362994 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362993 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362995 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362993 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362996 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362993 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362997 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362993 1075 #edb/ref 17592186362998 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362993 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362993 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362993 1079 #edb/ref 17592186362998 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362993 1080 #uuid "04472cee-3f9a-56c7-9b29-8748734c70cb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362994 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362994 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362994 1084 #uuid "44434ece-00fb-51cd-8a49-e2cfd67708d7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362995 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362995 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362995 1084 #uuid "0fc1ea08-fb0f-5011-824b-be7b928db8cd" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362996 1081 "\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362996 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362996 1084 #uuid "e3196088-1e84-5e59-ad8d-fd14cb623f3d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362997 1081 "1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362997 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362997 1084 #uuid "098ccdac-dc81-5c2f-9cf5-304766334c8d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362998 1081 "2\\pi " 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362998 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362998 1084 #uuid "5a0001fe-55b6-5233-a81e-3c1adda6f315" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362999 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363000 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362999 1069 "q-162491" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362999 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362999 1071 "Change the order of integration in the integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{z}}^{\\sqrt{3}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nso that it is integrated first with respect to $z,$ then $y,$ and then $x.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362999 1072 #uuid "6d111f5a-3dcb-5a81-9b5a-d0ae8da926cf" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186362999 1074 "We wish to find limits of integration ${u}_{1}(x,z),$ ${u}_{2}(x,z),$ ${v}_{1}(z),$ ${v}_{2}(z),$ $a,$ and $b$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{z}}^{\\sqrt{3}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,y)}^{{u}_{2}(x,y)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the region of integration $R$ can be written as a type III region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,\\sqrt{z}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{3}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch the region. Since it is a type III region, we first sketch the projection onto the $xz$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nE={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}.\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/37/3771c3587542c781136e1802cf2ad809aaa7aff701328963572fe9296c1eb856.png)\n\nThen, the region $R$ is shown in the diagram below, where $\\sqrt{z}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{3}.$\n\n![](images/8e/8e2aeb803b0458864560f894c3ec8635c38ac4b9febeb172115f4b3216fc44a5.png)\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x$ to $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x,$ we write $R$ as a type I region and its projection $D$ onto the $xy$-plane as a type I *plane* region.\n\nTo visualize this, imagine firing an arrow through the region parallel to the $z$-axis and in the direction of increasing $z,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/38/385eed97efeb951228a44009faf76dc676f565204885c8f0df2cee0afc1657a8.png)\n\nThe arrow enters the region through the bottom boundary and leaves through the top boundary:\n\n- The top boundary of the region, written in the form $z=z(x,y),$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{z}\\,⟺\\,z={y}^{2}.\n$$\n\n- The bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nz=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le {y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/83/837b43fa43b6d160d0734a629f08bb415bd91f382b99dbd6a5c227dd46b98f29.png)\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I plane region in the $xy$-plane with the top curve given by $y=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n![](images/90/90dc40b39cd7a3fdfcff0469b1915dcd64811a16aad0dad452c8f57d4118546b.png)\n\nHence, we have that\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration so that it is integrated first with respect to $z,$ then $y,$ then $x,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{z}}^{3}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363000 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363001 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363000 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363002 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363000 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363003 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363000 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363004 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363000 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363005 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363000 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 131941