\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363012 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363012 1084 #uuid "6173604f-81f7-5348-a560-f1d1e33f0a56" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363013 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363014 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363013 1069 "q-162507" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363013 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363013 1071 "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{z/x}^{x}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n*Hint: Change the order of integration to $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$*" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363013 1072 #uuid "ef9be3a1-a324-5dc1-89fc-c3baad1d92c4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363013 1074 "We cannot integrate the given integral because we cannot find a simple antiderivative of the integrand. So, we change the order of integration.\n\nWe wish to find the limits of integration ${u}_{1}(x,y),$ ${u}_{2}(x,y),$ ${v}_{1}(x),$ ${v}_{2}(x),$ $a,$ and $b$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{z/x}^{x}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,y)}^{{u}_{2}(x,y)}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the region of integration $R$ can be written as a type III region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le {x}^{2},\\,\\,\\frac{z}{x}\\le y\\le x}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch the region. Since it is a type III region, we first sketch the projection onto the $xz$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nE={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le {x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/2b/2b4cc501b983d6786c2e27680955a7ffdba17ff139ad4d9bed4a268521d365d9.png)\n\nThen, the region $R$ is shown in the diagram below, where $\\frac{z}{x}\\le y\\le x.$\n\n![](images/5c/5c02178f02f39fa2ce2b27c0c51f58f33d9f2e7e54621e079e5645730cb20e56.png)\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x$ to $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x,$ we write $R$ as a type I region and its projection $D$ onto the $xy$-plane as a type I *plane* region.\n\nTo visualize this, imagine firing an arrow through the region parallel to the $z$-axis and in the direction of increasing $z,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/f4/f4c313659ca62d8d595fda91f53be9b10c6f7fa1105475b7e833d7f0a2e8acbe.png)\n\nThe arrow enters the region through the bottom boundary and leaves through the top boundary:\n\n- The bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nz=0.\n$$\n\n- The top boundary of the region, written in the form $z=z(x,y),$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{z}{x}\\,⟺\\,z=xy.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le xy},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/79/79c4044d76be693decc1125ec88b53c162a6f29b0e701e0125319955bbe02fa1.png)\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I plane region in the $xy$-plane with the top curve given by $y=x.$\n\n![](images/e1/e123941fc02ba0ff653feffd0cc9b3f778fcd1c01ad2656b658e98fbcbae8b98.png)\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{z/x}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{\\int }_{0}^{xy}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4})[{\\int }_{0}^{xy}\\text{d}z]\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4})[z]_{0}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}8xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4}){\\int }_{0}^{x}2y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4}){[{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4})\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{4})]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363014 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363015 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363014 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363016 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363014 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363017 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363014 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363018 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363014 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363019 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363014 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363014 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363014 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363019 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363014 1080 #uuid "6d862e66-b5e6-54f5-a53f-795a2bda3551" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363015 1081 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363015 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363015 1084 #uuid "b8c8f7e9-9f53-51d0-9b75-251f027df51f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363016 1081 "3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363016 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363016 1084 #uuid "8ee59a30-cfe4-5dc7-b601-e25cce4e0651" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363017 1081 "2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363017 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363017 1084 #uuid "dce91bfe-93a5-5537-98f1-901c59ae4858" 131941395334