 constant $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =4x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(6)^{2} & =4(0)-\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}+C \\\\ C & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =4x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+18 \\\\ {v}^{2} & =8x-{x}^{2}+36 \\\\ v & =\\pm \\sqrt{-{x}^{2}+8x+36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x,$ we have that $v(x)>0,$ so we can disregard the negative square root. Therefore,\n\n$$\nv(x)=\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}+8x+36}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the maximum velocity:\n\n$$\n{v}_{max}=v(4)=\\sqrt{-(4)^{2}+8(4)+36}=2\\sqrt{13}\\,m/s\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363061 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363062 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363061 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363063 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363061 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363064 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363061 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363065 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363061 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363066 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363061 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363061 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363061 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363065 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363061 1080 #uuid "95c44088-63d3-5d47-8f73-8487757bc6ec" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363062 1081 "8\\,m/s" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363062 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363062 1084 #uuid "ec26c32f-330e-5878-8370-d35956d6bd96" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363063 1081 "6\\,m/s" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363063 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363063 1084 #uuid "255624ce-60b8-5c54-9dfe-53912d1536ec" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363064 1081 "4\\sqrt{3}\\,m/s" 13194139533445 175921860