 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIn ascending order, $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363357 1072 #uuid "7046d61a-2100-5f6e-80e3-9459516462dc" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363357 1074 "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}x+2 & 2x & 4 \\\\ 3 & x & x+1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =(x+2)|\\begin{aligned}x & x+1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2x|\\begin{aligned}3 & x+1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}3 & x \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(x+2)(3x)-2x(8-x)+4(-x) \\\\  & =3x(x+2)-2x(8-x)-4x \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+6x-16x+2{x}^{2}-4x \\\\  & =5{x}^{2}-14x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-14x & =0 \\\\ x(5x-14) & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\,\\text{or}\\,x=\\frac{14}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{14}{5}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363358 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363359 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363358 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363358 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363358 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363359 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363358 1080 #uuid "113f8edf-ce63-5e3c-8e20-25df8fcc000b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363359 1081 "0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363359 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363359 1084 #uuid "5e337463-b3e6-57c5-a2b0-3b2f8be1327c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363360 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363361 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363360 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363360 1077 "field-2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363360 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363361 13194139533445 17