{′}=f(x,y,z),\\, & z(a)=d,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbefore applying the update rule component-wise to each equation.\n\nTo apply Euler’s method, we first isolate ${y}^{″}$ so it can serve as the derivative of a new variable $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}+4x{y}^{′}-2y & ={x}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{″} & =-4x{y}^{′}+2y+{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variable $z={y}^{′}$ and ${z}^{′}={y}^{″}$ in the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}=-4xz+2y+{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that the initial value of $z$ is $z(0)={y}^{′}(0)=-1.$\nSo, the initial value problem reduces to the following system of first-order ODEs:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=z,\\, & y(0)=2, \\\\ {z}^{′}=-4xz+2y+{x}^{2},\\, & z(0)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can proceed with Euler's method by applying the update rule component-wise.\n\nFirst, because the initial conditions are $y(0)=2$ and $z(0)=-1,$ we place $y=2$ and $z=-1$ in the table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ |  |  | $-1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute both ${y}^{′}$ and ${z}^{′}$ according to the given rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =z=-1 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =-4xz+2y+{x}^{2} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 0\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 2+{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $-1$ |  | $-1$ | $4$ |  |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy$ and $Δz$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-1 \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ | $4$ | $4$ |\n\nTo get the new values of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x,$ $Δy$ to $y,$ and $Δz$ to $z,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+1=1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=2+(-1)=1 \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=-1+4=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these values to our table in a new row gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ | $4$ | $4$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ |  |  | $3$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n$y(1)≈1.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363441 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363442 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363441 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363441 1077 "field-3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363441 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363442 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363441 1080 #uuid "0140e720-f76b-520b-aa24-31f9d388b7ec" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363442 1081 "1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363442 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363442 1084 #uuid "87c6a003-fe91-5a09-a621-17ee211874e3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363443 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363444 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363443 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363443 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363443 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363444 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363443 1080 #uuid "7dcb8e82-9094-5e4b-8cf2-9b57be7acd86" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363444 1081 "-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363444 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363444 1084 #uuid "abecd009-0855-5118-a859-998bbc8be6cb" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363445 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363446 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363445 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [1759218