ng to the given rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =z=1 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =\\frac{2x+yz}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 1}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $1$ |  | $1$ | $2$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δy$ and $Δz$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $2$ |\n\nTo get the new values of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x,$ $Δy$ to $y,$ and $Δz$ to $z,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=1+1=2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=0+1=1 \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=1+2=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these values to our table in a new row gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $2$ |\n| $2$ | $1$ |  |  | $3$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n$y(2)≈1$\nand\n${y}^{′}(2)=z(2)≈3.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363454 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363453 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363453 1077 "field-2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363453 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363454 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363453 1080 #uuid "5b52f502-4acf-5a6a-8b06-3177235e9bf7" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363454 1081 "3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363454 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363454 1084 #uuid "bf0319dc-59f2-5297-90e8-74471efe