egin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}^{′}(t) & {x}_{2}^{′}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ and ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$ from $\\text{L3},$ we substitute each derivative into the matrix to get\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ A{x}_{1}(t) & A{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by substitution from $\\text{L2}\\text{ and }\\text{L3}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ From $\\text{L6}$ we have\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)].\n$$\n\nUsing the definition $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$ from $\\text{L1},$ we substitute to obtain\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=AΦ(t).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by substitution from $\\text{L1}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363540 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363541 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363542 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363543 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363539 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363539 1077 "field-2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363539 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363540 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363539 1080 #uuid "3a13d5b5-5298-5a70-9317-9289780933f2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363540 1081 "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363540 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363540 1084 #uuid "af1db821-3c70-5204-8966-bfafe5646081" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363541 1081 "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363541 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363541 1084 #uuid "46a98a5b-5103-59