 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${y}_{p}(0)=0$ because the particular solution is a sine series.\n\nNext, we use the derivative condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0.$ First, we compute the derivative of the total solution (with $A=0$):\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)∼B\\sqrt{2}\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\pi x)+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{n{\\pi }^{2}(18-{n}^{2})}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nApplying ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ and noting that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =B\\sqrt{2}\\pi +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{n{\\pi }^{2}(18-{n}^{2})} \\\\ B\\sqrt{2}\\pi  & =-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{n{\\pi }^{2}(18-{n}^{2})} \\\\ B & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{n{\\pi }^{2}(18-{n}^{2})} \\\\  & =-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{\\sqrt{2}{\\pi }^{3}(18-{n}^{2})} \\\\  & =-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}(-1)^{n}}{n{\\pi }^{3}(18-{n}^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $B$ back into ${y}_{c}=B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\pi x)$, we find the missing part:\n\n$$\ny(x)∼-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\pi x){\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}(-1)^{n}}{n{\\pi }^{3}(18-{n}^{2})}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{18(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{3}(18-{n}^{2})}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363735 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363736 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363735 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363737 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363735 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363738 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363735 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363739 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363735 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363735 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363735 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363738 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363735 1080 #uuid "e77f080d-827b-51df-b338-49