,$ calculate the maximum velocity ${v}_{\\text{max}}$ of the particle and determine the time when the particle reaches its maximum velocity. Do not round your answer.\n\nThe maximum velocity ${v}_{\\text{max}}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ is reached at $t=$\n{{field-2}}$\\text{s}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363796 1072 #uuid "01deaa82-6ed4-5ec3-bb26-dc6ad125e782" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363796 1074 "The extrema of the velocity $v$ occur at the critical points of $v.$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=a(t),$ to find the times where $v$ is a maximum, we just need to solve $a(t)=0$ and test each solution using the first or second derivative test.\n\nSolving $a(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =0 \\\\ 7-7{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 7(1-t)(1+t) & =0 \\\\ t & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t⩾0$, the extremum of the velocity function occurs when $t=1\\,\\text{s}.$\n\nWe now test the extreme value using the second derivative test. For this, we find the second derivative of $v(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}v}{\\text{d}{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(a(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7-7{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =-14t \\\\ {v}^{″}(1) & =-14(1) \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${v}^{″}(1)<0,$ we conclude that the velocity is maximized when $t=1\\,\\text{s}.$\n\nNow, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (7-7{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =7t-\\frac{7}{3}{t}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(2)=1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(2)-\\frac{7}{3}(2)^{3}+C & =1 \\\\ 14-\\frac{56}{3}+C & =1\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{17}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{17}{3}+7t-\\frac{7}{3}{t}^{3}.$\n\nFinally, we calculate the maximum velocity:\n\n$$\n{v}_{\\text{max}}=v(1)=\\frac{17}{3}+7(1)-\\frac{7}{3}(1)^{3}=\\frac{31}{3}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}\n$$\n\nSo the maximum velocity ${v}_{\\text{max}}=\\frac{31}{3}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ is reached at $t=1\\,\\text{s}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363797 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363798 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363797 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363797 1077 "field-1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363797 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363798 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363797 1080 #uuid "5ac3bdfa-2313-5db4-aa3b-2fcdafe606ef" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363798 1081 "\\frac{31}{3}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363798 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363798 1084 #uuid "f80921a7-9ef8-51bc-ba03-c610b343031b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363799 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363800 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363799 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363799 1077 "field-2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363799 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363800 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363799 1080 #uuid "9019baa6-75df-546b-b37a-ca7344b0b1e1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363800 1081 "1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363800 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363800 1084 #uuid "e86f0a56-8589-5937-b33b-d876d2fcde71" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363801 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363802 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363801 1069 "q-355263" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363801 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363801 1071 "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration