[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{12} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363919 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363920 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363919 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363921 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363919 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363922 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363919 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363923 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363919 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363924 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363919 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363919 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363919 1079 #edb/ref 17592186363924 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363919 1080 #uuid "974cc47c-a0cf-5ce6-8700-2a3f5c0bccd1" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363920 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363920 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363920 1084 #uuid "ce4106d4-3066-525e-9cc4-3cc62600cc77" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363921 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363921 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363921 1084 #uuid "30e731b8-e203-5d2a-b715-03aab570da25" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363922 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363922 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363922 1084 #uuid "c0ec102b-6380-5917-b3e8-96986912f2e4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363923 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363923 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363923 1084 #uuid "353ce806-e08a-585e-aedc-1f31c4ef4e92" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363924 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363924 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363924 1084 #uuid "88d5a945-073b-5c18-9a22-28e2025b07d3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363925 1068 #edb/ref 17592186363926 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363925 1069 "q-40745" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363925 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363925 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B={{u}_{1},{u}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an **orthonormal** basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $|a|+|b|+|c|?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363925 1072 #uuid "dbf56628-94da-5878-ab0e-12187baa0d83" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363925 1074 "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{3\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 0+4\\cdot 2}{{4}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize each vector to get an orthonormal basis.\n\n- ${u}_{1}=\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- ${u}_{2}=\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthonormal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=-\\frac{1}{3},$ $b=\\frac{2}{3},$ $c=\\frac{2}{3}$ and  \n\n$$\n|a|+|b|+|c|=|-\\frac{1}{3}|+|\\frac{2}{3}|+|\\frac{2}{3}|=\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363927 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186363926 1075 #edb/ref 17592