92186364081 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364082 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364081 1069 "q-76108" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364081 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364081 1071 "Consider the function $f(x)={2}^{x}+1.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(5).$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364081 1072 #uuid "67a843ac-f40c-59da-8377-455b0890a108" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364081 1074 "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(5),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(5)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(5))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(5).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(5)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(5) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =5 \\\\ {2}^{x}+1 & =5 \\\\ {2}^{x} & =4 \\\\ {2}^{x} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{-1}(5)=2.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={2}^{x}+1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot {2}^{x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(5) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(5))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364082 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364083 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364082 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364084 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364082 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364085 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364082 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364086 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364082 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364087 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364082 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364082 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [175921