8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364186 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364187 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364186 1069 "q-81212" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364186 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364186 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364186 1072 #uuid "fbde2955-a5db-5798-a76a-665975736935" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364186 1074 "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$ \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{5\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 3}{(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=6,$ $b=\\frac{9}{2},$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{(6)}{(\\frac{9}{2})}=\\frac{4}{3}.\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364187 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364188 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364187 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364189 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364187 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364190 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364187 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364191 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364187 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364192 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364187 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364187 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364187 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364188 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364187 1080 #uuid "a1b294cd-0690-5b2a-8b79-bfdfd5228580" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364188 1081 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364188 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364188 1084 #uuid "3a1f7f88-f4d6-55ab-96bb-e95b8529508e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364189 1081 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364189 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364189 1084 #uuid "761d56bb-9090-5642-9a0c-e14547f22359" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364190 1081 "27" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364190 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364190 1084 #uuid "8c80468f-7fc8-5012-914f-f4ac6b573a98" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364191 1081 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364191 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364191 1084 #uuid "3b1145a6-cf7a-5bfb-b5d9-39965f8e4d5f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364192 1081 "18" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [