igned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =A(j)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/4e/4e0e5c9cee037bded1f5739af35c3a8acfaa4d4e6f469b3e50afe69b96990e39.png)\n\nSo, the matrix represents a rotation of $\\pi $ radians (counterclockwise or clockwise) about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ (counterclockwise or clockwise) by an angle of $\\pi $ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](images/35/358dcedefd029cdbd07f3c64b1264e568bfbac134b92a607e9d55c632c277b13.png)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364207 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364208 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364207 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364209 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364207 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364210 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364207 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364211 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364207 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364212 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364207 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364207 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364207 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364212 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364207 1080 #uuid "e78ce83e-7416-5a1d-926b-9005c4697cd2" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364208 1081 "images/e6/e6a72b4fb4a9c100996e7761407a2eb923d22f0d26832964bea2d4d6e3c90f2e.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364208 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364208 1084 #uuid "5e3b14f5-b75f-5e25-8b24-54bca66e3bc4" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364209 1081 "images/3a/3a7e4f6e534ec77a08e425b86d97f43535c376909c80aa6621d0061ce1127b45.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364209 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 