"q-95397" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364436 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364436 1071 "Consider the change of variables given by the matrix equation\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand the curve $C,$ defined as\n\n$$\nC:\\,{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+4\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1}=4.\n$$\n\n \n\nGiven that the change of variables above reduces $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ to its canonical (diagonal) form $2{y}_{1}^{2}$ what type of a quadratic curve is defined by $C?$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364436 1072 #uuid "3c25a282-f09e-5080-ae4d-6a92631e6519" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364436 1074 "First, we note the following:\n\n$$\nC:\\,{{{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}+4\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1}=4\n$$\n\nLet's write the given change of variables explicitly:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{1}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{1}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the given change of variables reduces $Q(x)$ to its canonical form. Therefore, performing the change of variables on $C,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+4\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1} & =4 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}^{2}+4\\sqrt{2}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{1}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2}) & =4 \\\\ 2{y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{1}-4{y}_{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we complete the square for the variable ${y}_{1}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{1}-4{y}_{2} & =4 \\\\ 2({y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{1})-4{y}_{2} & =4 \\\\ 2({y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{1}+1-1)-4{y}_{2} & =4 \\\\ 2({y}_{1}+1)^{2}-2\\cdot 1-4{y}_{2} & =4 \\\\ 2({y}_{1}+1)^{2} & =4{y}_{2}+6 \\\\ 2({y}_{1}+1)^{2} & =4({y}_{2}+\\frac{3}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, performing the change of variables \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{z}_{1}={y}_{1}+1, \\\\ {z}_{2}={y}_{2}+\\frac{3}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({y}_{1}+1)^{2} & =4({y}_{2}+\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\ 2{z}_{1}^{2} & =4{z}_{2} \\\\ {z}_{1}^{2} & =2{z}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis represents a parabola that opens in the direction of the positive ${z}_{2}$-axis." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364437 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364438 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364437 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364439 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364437 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364440 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364437 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364441 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364437 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364442 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364437 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364437 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364437 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364440 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364437 1080 #uuid "23070fd2-4a47-5c26-ae55-52058929b2df" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364438 1081 "A pair of intersecting lines" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364438 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364438 1084 #uuid "b13d7123-12c3-5fba-865d-79d04d134405" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364439 1081 "An empty set" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364439 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364439 1084 #uuid "9eb75fec-aad0-52b8-8f0b-256603947924" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364440 1081 "A p