17592186364477 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364477 1071 "Find the orthogonal projection matrix that maps $x\\in {R}^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364477 1072 #uuid "04f2e807-374a-54f0-9c1c-c36bd677ab53" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364477 1074 "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nMoreover, ${u}_{i}\\cdot {u}_{i}^{T}$ is the projection matrix corresponding to ${u}_{i}.$\n\nFirst, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to $\\lambda =-1.$ Computing $A-(-1)I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+I & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{2}{3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=3,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖v‖=\\sqrt{13}.$ Dividing $v$ by its norm, we obtain the normalized eigenvector: \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, the required orthogonal projection matrix is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {u}^{T} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364478 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364479 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364478 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364480 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364478 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364481 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364478 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364482 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364478 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364483 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364478 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364478 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364478 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364482 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364478 1080 #uuid "114fa9c1-9d2d-5e26-8ec3-22bb6c29182d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364479 1081 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364479 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364479 1084 #uuid "0aff604c-8612-5d59-a83a-b4bff7afa693" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364480 1081 "\\sqrt{13}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364480 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364480 1084 #uuid "4ba28056-be96-5bb5-9d00-cdb75f7c223c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17