nd the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1}}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{6}{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** We find the vector ${v}_{3}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{3}{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{4}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=-1,$ $c=2,$ and $\\frac{a}{c}=\\frac{(-1)}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364505 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364506 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364505 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364507 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364505 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364508 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364505 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364509 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364505 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364510 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364505 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364505 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364505 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364506 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364505 1080 #uuid "ec4508d7-0dd6-5