$ is the standard matrix of $T$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364580 1072 #uuid "cbb0c470-3f82-5cd2-8de9-680715504460" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364580 1074 "Recall that a linear transformation $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto  ${R}^{2}$ if and only if \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=2\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, The condition $\\text{rank}(T)=2$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\text{Im}(T)={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, $T$ is surjective and so  $⟨-1,0⟩\\in \\text{Im}(T).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the condition $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)={0}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have that \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364581 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364582 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364581 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364583 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364581 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364584 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364581 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364585 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364581 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364586 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364581 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364581 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364581 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364585 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364581 1080 #uuid "f6804d75-0020-58f0-8b84-9333fc254a08" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364582 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364582 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364582 1084 #uuid "9b451578-e603-50dd-b11b-c2107467a062" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364583 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364583 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364583 1084 #uuid "d851680b-8402-55ea-9cf9-6b5b8d76c8b5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364584 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364584 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364584 1084 #uuid "4c902603-f774-5553-9e49-5c9b8260e30b" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364585 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364585 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364585 1084 #uuid "8f550d65-6f58-50f8-b2f2-f75e02a5849c" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364586 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364586 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364586 1084 #uuid "2c075842-d336-52cb-ba85-39faff17c3db" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364587 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364588 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364587 1069 "q-97079" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364587 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364587 1071 "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ onto the line $y=2x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $⟨2,1⟩\\in \\text{Im}(T)$\n- $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}$\n- $\\text{nullity}(T)=2$, where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364587 1072 #uuid "2335439b-17b4-5a3d-b1ce-91063205bf0d" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364587 1074 "Recall that when the image of a linear transformation $T$ in ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T$ is a one-dimensional line, then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=1,\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The point $(2,1)$ does not satisfy the equation of the line $y=2x$ since $1\\ne 2\\cdot 2.$ Hence, \n\n$$\n⟨2,1⟩\\notin \\text{Im}(T).\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{nullity}(T)=1,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have that \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364588 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364589 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364588 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364590 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364588 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364591 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364588 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364592 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364588 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364593 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364588 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364588 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364588 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364593 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364588 1080 #uuid "75652cd4-0892-5806-a1ea-d4a0fbeef0e3" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364589 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364589 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364589 1084 #uuid "8bd3c353-ce85-5793-ad0a-21270c2bf2c6" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364590 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364590 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364590 1084 #uuid "42ac35a1-0b22-54d2-9748-1ded75925c08" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364591 1081 "I only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364591 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364591 1084 #uuid "dd8f4106-c2cf-52ca-b819-cb85426cd1f0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364592 1081 "III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364592 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364592 1084 #uuid "88ea8cad-8bc9-500e-80e4-725520571421" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364593 1081 "II only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364593 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364593 1084 #uuid "9621e2c5-545b-5195-8075-b7593ac3fa11" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364594 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364595 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364594 1069 "q-98315" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364594 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364594 1071 "Which of the following curves is closed?" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364594 1072 #uuid "baf675cb-8cad-5a6a-ac62-d50434c21dd8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364594 1074 "A curve is closed if its terminal point coincides with its initial point.\n\nOf the given options, the only that satisfies the definition is the following:\n\n![](images/ba/baac4664b66df2d0e86f52fcd9d521f85464e42782e2bfadf66bd9dad8320854.png)" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364595 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364596 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364595 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364597 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364595 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364598 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364595 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364599 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364595 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364600 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364595 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364595 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364595 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364598 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364595 1080 #uuid "257d0ab5-242d-510d-bd46-e9e76adc2a12" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364596 1081 "images/7c/7c47f46496b3e4fcd6e09d374b86a1f2449248bdaffb1e54a70dd5be671c9b6a.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364596 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364596 1084 #uuid "ad3f2c6e-68b4-58bc-b1b8-f3b935fdf5e8" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364597 1081 "images/0f/0f388fc9c0aaae8535fd0b704b3ed84884aedf0462929ac2fdcc489889e6cb6b.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364597 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364597 1084 #uuid "92738762-df8f-5c3b-9019-5f385f994584" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364598 1081 "images/ba/baac4664b66df2d0e86f52fcd9d521f85464e42782e2bfadf66bd9dad8320854.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364598 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364598 1084 #uuid "262b5ada-7843-5256-8a22-32394ac71fd5" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364599 1081 "images/1c/1cc60dd2a4a40b025d421c91eea61228fb94f257adc870931800b249b6c2e43b.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364599 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364599 1084 #uuid "e6f9ba40-0d47-550d-a25d-76d4b7d0b216" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364600 1081 "images/7b/7bfab79811ce6721f783fd83751f5086b174679c6185ed1014ba621005372856.png" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364600 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364600 1084 #uuid "e602f6ed-d0aa-5ea9-8c9a-d2e9ef8d8f7f" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364601 1068 #edb/ref 17592186364602 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364601 1069 "q-9835" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364601 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364601 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $D$ given below?\n\n- $det(D)=1$\n- $D$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(D)=0$\n\n \n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364601 1072 #uuid "2e3acb77-06f5-5592-8e02-3140d23a412e" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364601 1074 "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(28-30)-2(7-5)+3(6-4) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-2-4+6 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(D)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true." 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364602 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364603 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364602 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364604 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364602 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364605 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364602 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364606 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364602 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364607 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364602 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364602 1077 "selection" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364602 1079 #edb/ref 17592186364603 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364602 1080 #uuid "e7423499-9165-54aa-b967-2b965343f4f0" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364603 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364603 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533445 17592186045585 true] [17592186364603 1084 #uuid "b2bfde12-85fe-5bb2-a31d-8f1490a205e7" 13194139